 "notes": "I read 37 stations on lines 1161–1197, one printed line each. 27 are starred and 10 are not. The list has no map numbers and no light characters. The coast is taken from the section heading \"EAST COAST OF ENGLAND\", but the list also includes Kent/Channel stations (Nore, Forelands, Gull, East Side) and two Channel Islands lights: Hanois \"(Guernsey)\" and Casquets \"(Alderney)\".\n\nHow I copied things:\n- Fragments are each line with its two-space indent removed. The spacing between the name and keeper columns is kept as printed.\n- Each keeper entry ends with a full stop. I treated that as punctuation closing the entry and left it off the last name (\"Thomas O. Hall & James W. Parsons.\" gives \"Thomas O. Hall\" and \"James W. Parsons\").\n- Names joined by \"&\" are split into separate keepers.\n- Line 1178: \"William Rees (mate)\" is recorded as keeper \"William Rees\", with \"(mate)\" in other.\n- Line 1172, Llyn Wells L.V.: \"The Principal.\" is a title, not a name, so I put it in other and left keepers empty. Move it to keepers if your roll should include unnamed principal keepers.\n- Line 1161, Longstone: it has both the star and the †, printed as \"*Longstone L.H.†\"; marks are given as \"*†\". The † refers to the note above the list: \"For nature of light, and position and description of station, see report for 1880.\" No other station in this list has the †.\n- Line 1163: I kept \"No. 5 Buoy, Teesmouth\" whole as the name with place null. \"No. 5\" is part of the light-vessel's name, not a map number.\n- Hanois and Casquets: place is given without the brackets; the text prints \"(Guernsey)\" and \"(Alderney)\". \"Spurn (Newsand)\" keeps its brackets because they are part of the name.\n\nRows to check:\n- Line 1186, Kentish Knock: printed with no type and no star. It is a light-vessel, but type is null as printed.\n- Two separate stations are called \"Hasbro'\": the L.V. (line 1175, starred) and the L.H. (line 1177, not starred).\n- The unstarred rows (Leman & Ower, Hasbro' L.H., Kentish Knock, Nore, North Foreland, North Sand Head, South Foreland, Casquets) have no keeper named, as the lead-in leads you to expect.\n\nSpellings kept as printed:\n- \"Llyn Wells\" (usually Lynn Well)\n- \"Languard Point\" (Landguard)\n- \"Hasbro'\" (Happisburgh)\n- \"Inner Farne\" (the heading example gives \"Farn, Inner,\"; this list uses \"Inner Farne\")\n- \"Orfordness\"\n- \"Newarp\"\n- \"Perfrement\"\n- \"Bonken\"\n- \"Wm. Wilby Woodruff\"\n- \"Edward le Gallais\" (lower-case \"le\")\n- \"W. Edwards\" (initial only)",
